import AxQM.Postulates.API.FourGateReachableCircuit
import AxQM.Core.FourGateReachableWireSubmonoid
import AxQM.Core.FourGateReversibleWireTower

/-!
# The whole register reachable circuit submonoid, as four-gate circuits on the tower
(N&C Exercise 4.43, whole-submonoid register lift onto the control tower)

The universality argument of Exercise 4.43 exhibits the *abstract* reachable circuit set
of `Concrete.exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_reachableCircuits` — dense in `U(2ⁿ⁺¹)` up to a global
phase — as circuits of the `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` gates. Its register-side counterpart,
the submonoid `reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ` of `Evolution (qudit 2ⁿ⁺¹)`
(`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableCircuit.lean`), is identified operator-by-operator with the
matrix reachable circuit set (`exists_reachableCircuitEvolution_op_eq`). This file **lifts that
whole
register submonoid onto the control tower `qtower n qubit`**, re-expressing each of its members as a
circuit whose generators are gates on individual tower wires.

The two generating families of `reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ` each have a tower
re-expression:

* the per-wire reachable single-qubit rotations `reachableRotationWireEvolutions n j θ`, by the
  whole-submonoid rotation lift `exists_reachableRotationGate_congr_quditPowTower_eq`
  (`AxQM/Core/FourGateReachableWireSubmonoid.lean`): transported by `quditPowTower n`, each member
  is `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n j.rev E` for a reachable rotation gate
  `E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ` (an `{H, S}`-conjugate of the measurement-realised `R_z(θ)`,
  Exercise 4.41);
* the `≤ 2`-control reversible gates `mcNotWireEvolution (n+1) S t ht`, by the reversible register
  lift `quditPowTower_congr_mcNotWireEvolution` (`AxQM/Core/FourGateReversibleWireTower.lean`):
  transported by `quditPowTower n`, each is the `mcNotTowerGate n (S.map rev) t.rev _` — the
  `placedMcNot` (a `Toffoli`/`CNOT`/`NOT` for `|S| ≤ 2`) on the reversed tower wire set.

This file assembles the two into one tower submonoid and transports the *whole* register
submonoid into it, one member at a time.

## What is formalised

* `reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ` — the **tower circuit submonoid**: the submonoid of
  `Evolution (qtower n qubit)` generated by the single-tower-wire reachable rotation gates
  `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i E` (`E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ`, over every wire `i`) together
  with the `≤ 2`-control reversible tower gates `mcNotTowerGate n S t ht` (`|S| ≤ 2`,
  `t ∉ S`). Every generator is a genuine circuit of the `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` gates on
  a tower wire (rotations: `{H, S}`-conjugates of the Exercise 4.41 measurement circuit
  `rzThreeFifthsCircuit`; reversible: `placedMcNot` = `Toffoli`/`CNOT`/`NOT`) — the tower
  counterpart of the register submonoid `reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ`.
* `congr_quditPowTower_mem_reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions` — **the whole-submonoid tower lift**:
  every member `E` of the register submonoid `reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ`, transported onto the
  control tower via the register bridge `quditPowTower n`, lies in the tower submonoid:

    `Evolution.congr (quditPowTower n) E ∈ reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ`.

  Proved by `Submonoid.closure_induction`. On a generator: a per-wire rotation member (wire `j`)
  maps by the rotation lift `exists_reachableRotationGate_congr_quditPowTower_eq` to
  `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n j.rev E` (`E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ`), a generator of the tower
  submonoid; a reversible generator `mcNotWireEvolution (n+1) S t ht` (`|S| ≤ 2`) maps by
  `quditPowTower_congr_mcNotWireEvolution` to `mcNotTowerGate n (S.map rev) t.rev _`, whose reversed
  control set still has `card ≤ 2` (`Finset.card_map`) and excludes the reversed target
  (`Finset.mem_map_equiv`) — a generator too. The `1` / product cases are the monoid-homomorphism
  laws of `Evolution.congr` (`Evolution.congr_id` / `Evolution.congr_comp`) feeding `one_mem` /
  `mul_mem`. The whole-circuit analogue of the single-family rotation lift
  `exists_reachableRotationGate_congr_quditPowTower_eq`.

So every reachable register circuit is, on the tower, a circuit built entirely from the
four named gates `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` on individual tower wires. This is the register-lift step in
the universality theorem: the matrix density transported through `Matrix.toEuclideanCLM`
lands in the closure of the operator image of `reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ`
(`exists_reachableCircuitEvolution_op_eq`), which this lift re-expresses over the four-gate
tower gates.

The two half-lifts it assembles are `AxQM/Core/FourGateReachableWireSubmonoid.lean` (rotations) and
`AxQM/Core/FourGateReversibleWireTower.lean` (reversible).
-/

open scoped InnerProductSpace TensorProduct

noncomputable section

namespace AxQM

/-- **The tower circuit submonoid.** The submonoid of `Evolution (qtower n qubit)`
generated by the two tower generating families: the single-tower-wire reachable single-qubit
rotation gates `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i E` (`E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ`, over every wire
`i`) and the `≤ 2`-control reversible tower gates `mcNotTowerGate n S t ht` (`|S| ≤ 2`,
`t ∉ S`). Each generator is a genuine circuit of the `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` gates on a
tower wire — the tower counterpart of the register submonoid
`reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ` (`congr_quditPowTower_mem_reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions`). -/
noncomputable def reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions (n : ℕ) (θ : ℝ) :
    Submonoid (Evolution (qtower n qubit)) :=
  Submonoid.closure
    ((⋃ i : Fin (n + 1),
        (Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i '' (reachableRotationGates θ : Set (Evolution qubit)))) ∪
      {E | ∃ (S : Finset (Fin (n + 1))) (t : Fin (n + 1)) (ht : t ∉ S),
        S.card ≤ 2 ∧ E = mcNotTowerGate n S t ht})

/-- **The whole register reachable circuit submonoid lifts to tower circuits.** Every
member `E` of the register-level reachable circuit submonoid `reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ`,
transported onto the control tower via the register bridge `quditPowTower n`, lies in the
tower circuit submonoid:

  `Evolution.congr (quditPowTower n) E ∈ reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ`.

Proved by `Submonoid.closure_induction` over `reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ`. On a generator: a
per-wire reachable-rotation member (wire `j`) is carried by the rotation whole-submonoid lift
`exists_reachableRotationGate_congr_quditPowTower_eq` to `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n j.rev E` for
a reachable rotation gate `E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ` — a generator of the tower submonoid (at
wire `i = j.rev`); a `≤ 2`-control reversible generator `mcNotWireEvolution (n+1) S t ht` is carried
by the reversible register lift `quditPowTower_congr_mcNotWireEvolution` to the
`mcNotTowerGate n (S.map Fin.revPerm.toEmbedding) t.rev _`, whose reversed control set again has
`card ≤ 2` (`Finset.card_map`) and excludes the reversed target (`Finset.mem_map_equiv`) — also a
generator. The `1` and product cases are the monoid-homomorphism laws of `Evolution.congr`
(`Evolution.congr_id` / `Evolution.congr_comp`, via `Evolution.one_def` / `Evolution.mul_def`),
landing in the tower submonoid by `one_mem` / `mul_mem`.

So every reachable register circuit is realised, on the tower, as a circuit built entirely
from `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` on individual tower wires — the register-lift step in the density
transport and the universality theorem. -/
theorem congr_quditPowTower_mem_reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions {n : ℕ} {θ : ℝ}
    {E : Evolution (qudit (2 ^ (n + 1)))} (hE : E ∈ reachableCircuitEvolutions n θ) :
    Evolution.congr (quditPowTower n) E ∈ reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ := by
  induction hE using Submonoid.closure_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    rcases hx with hrot | hperm
    · -- reachable single-qubit rotation on register wire `j`.
      rw [Set.mem_iUnion] at hrot
      obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hrot
      have hj' : x ∈ reachableRotationWireEvolutions n j θ := hj
      obtain ⟨G, hG, hGeq⟩ := exists_reachableRotationGate_congr_quditPowTower_eq hj'
      rw [hGeq]
      exact Submonoid.subset_closure
        (Or.inl (Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨j.rev, Set.mem_image_of_mem _ hG⟩))
    · -- `≤ 2`-control reversible register gate `mcNotWireEvolution (n+1) S t ht`.
      obtain ⟨S, t, ht, hcard, rfl⟩ := hperm
      rw [quditPowTower_congr_mcNotWireEvolution]
      refine Submonoid.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨S.map Fin.revPerm.toEmbedding, t.rev, ?_, ?_, rfl⟩)
      · rw [Finset.mem_map_equiv]; simpa using ht
      · rw [Finset.card_map]; exact hcard
  | one =>
    simpa only [Evolution.one_def, Evolution.congr_id] using
      one_mem (reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ)
  | mul x y _ _ ihx ihy =>
    rw [Evolution.mul_def x y, Evolution.congr_comp, ← Evolution.mul_def]
    exact mul_mem ihx ihy

end AxQM

end
